From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add headless --list-formats support for Scribus 1.7.4

Vibe coded by Codex

Add a --list-formats command that starts with Qt's offscreen platform,
loads only file-format and exporter plugins, and exits without creating
the main window, splash screen, scanning fonts, or initializing Python.

Report the runtime document/vector handlers and their capabilities,
extensions, MIME types, IDs, priorities and plugin names, plus image and
pattern imports, text importers, color palettes, built-in exports,
exporter plugin metadata, and Qt reader/writer codecs.

Also wait for the antiword capability probe to finish so listing text
importers does not emit a spurious QProcess destruction warning.

Rebased against scribus-1.7.4_pre20260918.tar.xz. Preserve the new
Wayland/XCB startup default and the split core initialization API.
---
